Subject: [PATCH 9/9] Decode tool arguments a CLI delivered as \uXXXX escapes

Reason: antigravity-cli 1.1.24 cannot put a non-ASCII character into a
`tools/call` argument. It spells every one of them as a literal `\uXXXX`
escape *inside* the JSON string, so the harness MCP server's `json.loads`
hands back the six characters of the escape instead of the character. Nothing
else in the frame is escaped -- quotes and backslashes are not doubled, and
`<` still arrives as the `\u003c` a correct serializer writes -- so this is
not a JSON string to parse twice; it is one transformation applied to the
non-ASCII characters alone. The whole answer therefore reaches the pipeline as
ASCII: a correction window measured 2026-09-04 submitted 5988 characters
carrying 815 backslashes, every one of them followed by `u`; the validator
judged `char_count` against a text three times its real length (45 weighted
characters where the model wrote 16), and every line of the delivered SRT read
`\u4f1d\u3048\u308b...`. The stage reported success throughout: nothing
downstream of `submit` can tell escaped text from text.

The repair sits where the frame enters the server, before the request
fingerprint and before any handler reads the arguments, and it is deliberately
narrow: an argument is decoded only when it is pure ASCII, carries such an
escape and yields a non-ASCII character by it. A driver that delivers its
arguments intact never matches, and text that meant to hold the six characters
`\u0041` decodes to ASCII and is left alone. Surrogate pairs are rejoined; a
lone surrogate leaves the argument untouched. The first repair in a process
says so on stderr, which lands in that capsule's `events/stderr.log`.

Removal: Delete once the CLI passes non-ASCII tool arguments through
unchanged (or once the harness stops taking answers over MCP).

diff --git a/src/finesub/llm/agent/agent_mcp_server.py b/src/finesub/llm/agent/agent_mcp_server.py
index 344ea9f..26441a0 100644
--- a/src/finesub/llm/agent/agent_mcp_server.py
+++ b/src/finesub/llm/agent/agent_mcp_server.py
@@ -41,6 +41,7 @@ from __future__ import annotations
 import hashlib
 import json
 import os
+import re
 import sys
 import time
 import uuid
@@ -325,6 +326,64 @@ def _page_end(text: str, offset: int, limit_bytes: int) -> int:
     return end
 
 
+# One `\uXXXX` escape as a CLI that cannot put a non-ASCII character into a
+# tool argument writes it (see `_unescaped_tool_text`).
+_ESCAPED_CODEPOINT = re.compile(r"\\u([0-9a-fA-F]{4})")
+_ESCAPE_REPAIR_REPORTED = False
+
+
+def _unescaped_tool_text(value: str) -> str:
+    r"""Repair one tool argument whose non-ASCII characters arrived escaped.
+
+    antigravity-cli 1.1.24 spells every non-ASCII codepoint of a `tools/call`
+    argument as a literal `\uXXXX` *inside* the JSON string, so `json.loads`
+    hands back the six characters of the escape instead of the character
+    (measured 2026-09-04: a `submit` payload arrived as 5988 ASCII characters
+    carrying 815 backslashes, every one of them followed by `u`, and that
+    window's subtitles reached the SRT as `\u4f1d\u3048...`). Only
+    the non-ASCII characters are treated this way -- quotes and backslashes are
+    not doubled -- so the argument is not a JSON string to parse, and the
+    escapes are decoded where they stand.
+
+    An argument is touched only when it is pure ASCII, carries such an escape
+    and yields a non-ASCII character by it: text that meant to hold the six
+    characters `\u0041` decodes to ASCII and is left alone, and a driver that
+    delivers its arguments intact never matches at all.
+    """
+
+    if not value.isascii() or "\\u" not in value:
+        return value
+    decoded = _ESCAPED_CODEPOINT.sub(lambda match: chr(int(match.group(1), 16)), value)
+    if any("\ud800" <= character <= "\udfff" for character in decoded):
+        # A character outside the BMP arrives as two escapes, one surrogate each.
+        try:
+            decoded = decoded.encode("utf-16", "surrogatepass").decode("utf-16")
+        except UnicodeError:
+            return value
+    return value if decoded.isascii() else decoded
+
+
+def _unescaped_arguments(value: Any) -> Any:
+    """`_unescaped_tool_text` over every string in one call's arguments."""
+
+    if isinstance(value, str):
+        repaired = _unescaped_tool_text(value)
+        if repaired is not value:
+            global _ESCAPE_REPAIR_REPORTED
+            if not _ESCAPE_REPAIR_REPORTED:
+                _ESCAPE_REPAIR_REPORTED = True
+                sys.stderr.write(
+                    "agent_mcp_server: this CLI escaped the non-ASCII characters "
+                    "of its tool arguments as \\uXXXX; decoding them\n"
+                )
+        return repaired
+    if isinstance(value, Mapping):
+        return {key: _unescaped_arguments(item) for key, item in value.items()}
+    if isinstance(value, Sequence) and not isinstance(value, (str, bytes, bytearray)):
+        return [_unescaped_arguments(item) for item in value]
+    return value
+
+
 def request_id_for(
     *,
     assignment_id: str,
@@ -483,6 +542,9 @@ class HarnessToolServer:
         if method == "tools/call":
             name = str(params.get("name") or "")
             arguments = params.get("arguments") if isinstance(params.get("arguments"), Mapping) else {}
+            # Before any handler reads them and before the request
+            # fingerprint: a repaired argument is the argument the model wrote.
+            arguments = _unescaped_arguments(arguments)
             return self._result(rpc_id, self._call(name, arguments, rpc_id=rpc_id))
         if rpc_id is None:
             return None
